# Architecture Source of Truth

Before implementing ANY feature, modifying ANY code, generating ANY file, or suggesting ANY architectural change, you MUST first read and understand:

1. docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md
2. docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md

These documents are the authoritative source of truth.

Never make assumptions that contradict these documents.

If implementation appears to conflict with the documents:

- stop
- explain the conflict
- ask whether the architecture should change

Never silently modify the architecture through code.

If information is missing, ask for clarification instead of inventing new structures.

Never introduce:

- new entities
- new relationships
- new database tables
- new modules
- new services

unless they already exist in the architecture documents.

If a new structure is required, explain why and request approval first.